India's Upcoming National Competitions (2026) and Their Participants

India hosts numerous national-level competitions every year that help students, innovators, athletes, and young leaders showcase their talent. These competitions provide opportunities for learning, scholarships, recognition, and career growth.

1. Bharatiya Antariksh Hackathon 2026

This national hackathon is organized by the Indian Space Research Organisation (ISRO) to encourage innovation in space science and technology. Participants work on real-world challenges related to aerospace, satellites, and space research.

Participants:

Engineering students
Science students
Technology enthusiasts
University teams
2. Vivo Ignite 2026

A national innovation competition based on the theme "Tech for Good". Students develop solutions for social and environmental problems using technology.

Participants:

School students (Classes 8–12)
Young innovators
Technology enthusiasts
3. Viksit Bharat Young Leaders Dialogue (VBYLD) 2026

An initiative under MY Bharat that encourages youth to develop solutions for national development in areas such as education, healthcare, sustainability, AI, and governance.

Participants:

College students
Young professionals
Start-up enthusiasts
Future policymakers
4. National Olympiads 2026

Olympiads test students' knowledge and problem-solving abilities in subjects such as Mathematics, Science, and Logical Reasoning.

Participants:

School students (Classes 1–10 and higher depending on the Olympiad)
Mathematics enthusiasts
Science enthusiasts

Examples:

National Level Mathematics Olympiad (NLMO)
National Level Science Olympiad (NLSO)
All India Talent Search Examination (AITSE)
5. YUVIKA 2026 (Young Scientist Programme)

ISRO's Young Scientist Programme introduces students to space science and technology through workshops and practical exposure.

Participants:

Primarily Class 9 students
Students interested in STEM and space research
6. AEROMANTHAN Bharat 2026

A national aerospace and defense simulation competition where students engage in strategic decision-making, research, and innovation projects.

Participants:

School students
Engineering students
Aerospace enthusiasts
Defense technology aspirants
7. Megathon 2026 – Innovation for Bharat

A nationwide innovation challenge focusing on Healthcare, Energy, Environment, Agriculture, and Deep Technology.

Participants:

Engineering students
Researchers
Start-up teams
Innovators
8. National Hackathons and Coding Competitions

Several institutions across India organize national-level hackathons and coding contests that encourage innovation and teamwork. Examples include Codefest and hardware hackathons such as PLUTONIUM 2026.

Participants:

Engineering students
Programmers
AI and Data Science students
Robotics enthusiasts
9. Khelo India Competitions

These competitions aim to identify and nurture sports talent across India. Athletes compete in various sports at state and national levels.

Participants:

School athletes
College athletes
Emerging sportspersons
National-level competitors
10. Pariksha Pe Charcha Contest 2026

A nationwide contest that gives students, teachers, and parents an opportunity to interact with the Prime Minister and share ideas on education and examinations.

Participants:

Students
Teachers
Parents
Conclusion

India's upcoming national competitions in 2026 cover a wide range of fields including:

Science and Technology
Artificial Intelligence
Space Research
Innovation and Entrepreneurship
Mathematics and Olympiads
Sports
Leadership and Governance

As a future AI & Data Science engineering student, competitions such as ISRO Hackathons, YUVIKA, Vivo Ignite, National Hackathons, Olympiads, and VBYLD can be especially valuable for building your profile, technical skills, and career opportunities.